{"name":"Blood Donor","hex":"#ea1822","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blood donor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who donates blood for use in transfusion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blood_donor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blood donation","blocks":[{"text":"A blood donation occurs when a person voluntarily has blood drawn and used for transfusions or made into blood products and biopharmaceutical medications by a process called fractionation. A donation may be of whole blood, or of specific components directly (apheresis). Blood banks often participate in the collection process as well as the procedures that follow it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Blood_donation_pictogram.svg/330px-Blood_donation_pictogram.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_donation"},{"title":"Blood","blocks":[{"text":"Blood is a specialized form of connective tissue and body fluid in the circulatory system of humans and other vertebrates that delivers necessary substances such as nutrients and oxygen to the cells of the body, and transports metabolic waste products away from those same cells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg/330px-Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood"},{"title":"Donor","blocks":[{"text":"A donor in general is a person, organization or government which donates something voluntarily. The term is usually used to represent a form of pure altruism, but is sometimes used when the payment for a service is recognized by all parties as representing less than the value of the donation and that the motivation is altruistic. In business law a donor is someone who is giving the gift (law), and a donee the person receiving the gift."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donor"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Saal_Blutspendezentrum_Basel_3.jpg/500px-Saal_Blutspendezentrum_Basel_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Saal_Blutspendezentrum_Basel_3.jpg/1280px-Saal_Blutspendezentrum_Basel_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Saal_Blutspendezentrum_Basel_3.jpg/500px-Saal_Blutspendezentrum_Basel_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blood donation center at the University Hospital of Basel, Switzerland. From left to right: Two cell separators for apheresis, secluded office for pre-donation blood pressure measurement and blood count, and on the right, chairs for whole blood donations.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaal_Blutspendezentrum_Basel_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Blooddonatio.jpg/500px-Blooddonatio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Blooddonatio.jpg/1280px-Blooddonatio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Blooddonatio.jpg/500px-Blooddonatio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A patient donating blood at a Blood  Bank in Córdoba, Argentina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlooddonatio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/BLOOD_DONATIONS_BY_AGE_GROUP.png/500px-BLOOD_DONATIONS_BY_AGE_GROUP.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/BLOOD_DONATIONS_BY